  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|3}=\\frac{1}{4}.$",
